10
00:57:30,000 --> 00:57:36,000
Trinity and Beyond: The Atomic Bomb Movie is a 1995 American documentary
film directed by Peter Kuran and narrated by William Shatner.

11
01:03:15,000 --> 01:03:21,000
Using restored archive footage, the film traces the development of nuclear weapons and their testing, from 
America's Trinity test of 1945 (hence the title) to the first Chinese atomic bomb test in 1964.

12
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
Kuran's commentary on the DVD version claims that the DVD replaces some
of the original footage with better-quality versions.

13
01:14:45,000 --> 01:14:51,000
There are some short special effects sequences too.

14
01:20:30,000 --> 01:20:36,000
The film has also since been released on Blu-ray.

15
01:26:15,000 --> 01:26:21,000
The film explores themes of atomic bomb,
energiestrahlenwaffe, atomic bomb test, nuclear explosion.
